 "title": "Master of Business Administration (Business Analytics) (MBA(BA)) | IIM Bangalore",
 "text": "DURATION\nTwo-year fulltime\nprogramme\n \nENROLLED IN 2026\n77 students\n \nDownload Brochure\n\nThe Post Graduate Programme in Business Analytics, leading to:\n\nMaster of Business Administration (Business Analytics)\n\nPost Graduate Programme in Business Analytics (PGPBA) is a masters level programme, leading to the grant of a degree of Master of Business Administration in Business Analytics. The two-year, full-time, residential programme is designed to equip students to take on leadership roles in using analytics and artificial intelligence to solve increasingly complex problems. It lasts six trimesters, spread over two years, with a summer project intermediary.\n\nClick here for MBA (Business Analytics) @ IIMB\n\nMessage from the Chairperson\n\nProfessor Manaswini Bhalla\n\nChairperson – Post Graduate Programme in Business Analytics\n\nWelcome to the Post Graduate Programme in Management (PGP) and the Post Graduate Programme in Business Analytics (PGP-BA).\n\nThe Post Graduate Programme in Business Analytics (PGPBA) is a programme built to develop future leaders with an analytical mindset and an understanding of the latest methodologies in analytics, allowing them to apply their learning across various functional areas of management. The curriculum of the program is a rigorous and taught by world-class faculty. Like the PGP programme, this program also allows students to develop holistically and ensures that the students get global exposure. The first year of the program has intensive course work with emphasis on analytical and mathematical skills followed by eight week summer internship. In the second year of the programme, students can choose from a variety of electives and opt for an exchange programme in select international business schools. Through the second year, PGPBA students are encouraged to take electives in the field of business analytics across the domain of management.\n\nThrough your time at IIM Bangalore, you will get opportunities to collaborate with and learn from your peers, and engage with the illustrious alumni of the Institute. At IIM Bangalore while we pursue the highest levels of academic rigour, integrity and ethical behaviour, we give equal importance to the virtues of empathy and collaboration. Your time here is bound to be a wholesome and life-changing experience.\n\nBachelors Discipline Profile 2026\nBachelorers Discipline\tNo. Of Candidates\tMale\tFemale\nEngineering\t60\t39\t21\nManagement\t5\t4\t1\nCommerce\t3\t2\t1\nScience\t8\t5\t3\nOthers\t1\t1\t \nMale\n51\nFemale\n26\nExperience in Month\tMale\tFemale\tTotal\nNo Experience\t7\t5\t12\n< 13\t3\t2\t5\n13 - 24\t9\t7\t16\n25 - 36\t19\t8\t27\n37 - 48\t12\t2\t14\nAbove 48\t1\t2\t3\nAge\tMale\tFemale\tTotal\n19-22\t10\t4\t14\n23 - 25\t27\t20\t47\n26 - 28\t14\t2\t16\nAbove 28\t-\t-\t-\nPGPBA in the News\nPGP, PGPBA and EPGP sweep No. 1 positions in India in QS MiM, BA and Global MBA Rankings 2027\nPragya 2026: IIM Bangalore faculty share their perspective on transition and new beginnings with PGP and PGPBA students nearing graduation\nThree IIM Bangalore MBAs reign #1 in India across QS World University Rankings 2026 portfolio\nAccreditation and Rankings\n\nStudent Achievements\nView all\n\nSnackWise startup by PGP ‘25 students selected for NSRCEL incubation\n\nPGP ’25 students crowned pan-India winners at Rajasthan Royals Case Competition\n\nPGP ’25 students clinch second runner-up at HDFC Life Case Competition\n\nStudent Testimonials\n\nAnusha S, PGPBA 2020-22\n\nBhanavi Luthra, PGPBA 2021-23\n\nSrinath Vigneshwar, PGPBA 2021-23\n\nPlacements\n\nDownload Our Placement Report 2026\n\nDownload PDF\n\nDisability Policy Statement\n\nThe Indian Institute of Management Bangalore (IIMB) endeavours to remove all barriers that prevent students with disabilities from realizing their potential. The objective of this policy is to provide “equal opportunity” for all students. IIMB commits to a time-bound programme to remove all barriers to access faced by students with disabilities. Access includes, but is not limited to:\n\nPhysical access to all parts of the campus used by students;\nAccess to teaching and reference material using appropriate technology wherever necessary;\nAccess to e-resources through the adoption of WCAG and other relevant standards.\n\nIIMB will assess the needs of each enrolled student with disability individually and determine what needs to be done to provide the best possible educational experience for that student. An Office of Disability Services will arrange such an assessment and be the nodal point to ensure that the needs of the student are communicated to every relevant office/department/person of IIMB and fulfilled appropriately.\n\nIIMB will take proactive steps to identify career opportunities for students with disabilities, and seek to influence recruiting organisations to adopt equal opportunity employment policies and practices.\n\nIIMB will strive to prevent discrimination against students with disabilities. IIMB will sensitise all relevant stakeholders to the needs and challenges of students with disabilities through periodic workshops and campaigns. Any discrimination against students with disabilities or rude/insensitive behaviour will be taken seriously, and could be cause for disciplinary action against the concerned faculty member, staff member, or student. While IIMB will follow the Persons with Disabilities Act and other legal provisions, the intent of this policy is to go beyond the legal requirements to provide a truly supportive environment to students with disabilities. As a first step towards this objective, IIMB has setup a “Committee on Disability” at the institute level that will provide leadership and focus. In the future, IIMB will form partnerships with industry bodies and reputed non- governmental organisations (NGOs) working in the field\n\nAdopted by IIMB Bangalore Faculty on July 15, 2009\n\nContact\n\nAdmissions Office\n\n+91-80-2699 3013 / 3017\n\npgpba.adm[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nPGPBA Programme Office\n\n+91-80-26993036\n\npgpoffice[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nStudent Affairs Council\n\nRead more",
